course: dictionary
lesson: 5056
title: Spotting an insect
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An insect is a small animal with six legs and a body in three parts: head, thorax and abdomen. Most insects also have wings and antennae. Read the clues in the sentence: «Like all insects, a beetle has six legs, three body parts and two feelers.» The clues tell you what an insect is.
explain: Use the same clues to check if something is not an insect. «A spider is not an insect: it has eight legs, two body parts and no antennae or wings.» A spider has too many legs to be an insect, so counting legs and body parts helps you decide.
explain: Ask yourself: does my meaning still fit the sentence? If you swap in «a small animal with six legs» for insect, «Ants, bees, butterflies, beetles and flies are insects» still makes sense.
fact: An insect has six legs and a body in three parts: head, thorax and abdomen.
fact: Most insects have wings and antennae, which are the feelers on the head.
fact: Ants, bees, butterflies, beetles and flies are all insects.
fact: Spiders are not insects: they have eight legs. A woodlouse is not an insect either, it is a relative of crabs.
fact: Some insects sting or bite, like bees, wasps and mosquitoes. If a sting makes you swell up or makes breathing hard, tell an adult straight away.
exercise: «Like all insects, a beetle has six legs, three body parts and two feelers.» How many legs does an insect have? | Eight | Ten | *Six | Four
exercise: «A spider is not an insect: it has eight legs, two body parts and no antennae or wings.» Which number of legs shows a spider is not an insect? | Four | Three | *Eight | Six
exercise: «Insects can also be fierce: a bombardier beetle fires a boiling puff with a pop.» What is a bombardier beetle? | A spider | A flower | A bird | *An insect
test: Which of these is an insect? | Crab | Spider | *Ant | Woodlouse
test: How many body parts does an insect have? | Two | Six | Four | *Three
exam: «A spider is not an insect: it has eight legs, two body parts and no antennae or wings.» Ants, bees and beetles are insects, so what is a spider? | *Not an insect | A kind of fly | An insect with extra legs | A kind of beetle
